{"name":"Wildflower Honey","hex":"#c69c5d","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"wildflower","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A wild (uncultivated) flowering plant.","A flower from such a plant."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wildflower"},{"term":"honey","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sweet, viscous, gold-colored fluid produced from plant nectar by bees, and often consumed by humans.","A variety of this substance."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Involving or resembling honey.","Of a pale yellow to brownish-yellow color, like most types of honey."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/honey"}],"entries":[{"title":"Wildflower","blocks":[{"text":"A wildflower is a flower that grows in the wild, rather than being intentionally seeded or planted. The term implies that the plant is neither a hybrid nor a selected cultivar that is any different from the native plant, even if it is growing where it would not naturally be found. The term can refer to the whole plant, even when not in bloom, and not just the flower."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/07/DwSixspecies.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wildflower","wikidata":"Q3585615"},{"title":"Honey","blocks":[{"text":"Honey is a sweet and viscous substance made by several species of bees, the best-known of which are honey bees. Honey is made and stored to nourish bee colonies. Bees produce honey by gathering and then refining the sugary secretions of plants or the secretions of other insects, like the honeydew of aphids. This refinement takes place both within individual bees, through regurgitation and enzymatic activity, and during storage in the hive, through water evaporation that concentrates the honey's sugars until it is thick and viscous."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/Runny_hunny.jpg/330px-Runny_hunny.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Honey","wikidata":"Q10987"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Wildflowers_western_australia.jpg/500px-Wildflowers_western_australia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Wildflowers_western_australia.jpg/500px-Wildflowers_western_australia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Wildflowers of Western Australia","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWildflowers_western_australia.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Grassland_Spring_Jewels%2C_Lake_Grapevine%2C_Texas_%28marcegottlieb_wikimedia%29.png/500px-Grassland_Spring_Jewels%2C_Lake_Grapevine%2C_Texas_%28marcegottlieb_wikimedia%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Grassland_Spring_Jewels%2C_Lake_Grapevine%2C_Texas_%28marcegottlieb_wikimedia%29.png/1280px-Grassland_Spring_Jewels%2C_Lake_Grapevine%2C_Texas_%28marcegottlieb_wikimedia%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Grassland_Spring_Jewels%2C_Lake_Grapevine%2C_Texas_%28marcegottlieb_wikimedia%29.png/500px-Grassland_Spring_Jewels%2C_Lake_Grapevine%2C_Texas_%28marcegottlieb_wikimedia%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Wildflowers are blooming in April in a field in central Texas near Lake Grapevine.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGrassland_Spring_Jewels%2C_Lake_Grapevine%2C_Texas_(marcegottlieb_wikimedia).png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Death_valley_flowers_1.jpg/500px-Death_valley_flowers_1.jpg?ut